Z||000006||maryjane||08-10-2001||05:20 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LAMBO:<BR><B>Maryjane, did your father ever put a v8 flathead in a Ford 8N tractor. They make a kit to attach the front axel to one. I've got an 8N just itchin' to have one.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Todd</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>No, I don't think so, tho we had lots of 8n's and 9n's around. He did take a car rearend and coupled a fh to the axle end. Turned the driiveshaft yoke straight down and put a big mower blade on it. Put on a little trailer frame & pulled it with the tractor. Even at idle, it turned so fast it would scare the sh** out of you.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> No guards or nothin. That's when us kids went together and bought him a bush hog.He and my uncle used to race a 49 or 50 mdl Ford out at the old Buffalo Speedway in Houston.<BR>||||reg||1
