Z||000014||Songman||08-12-2001||11:05 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LAMBO:<BR><B>Maryjane, did your father ever put a v8 flathead in a Ford 8N tractor. They make a kit to attach the front axel to one. I've got an 8N just itchin' to have one.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Todd</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>My girlfriend's dad has a 9N he is rebuilding. I found a guy in SC that has all sorts of parts for them, brand new! I e-mailed him and he said he could sell me the complete grille, hood, and side parts for under $300! He's somewhere in SC. I found him on eBay.<P>Back on topic...<P>We always used Champion plugs in the old days. I think they were the best back then. I use AC Delco now. I wasted all that money buying fancy plugs and found them to be just hype.<P>As for batteries, nothing but Diehard. Been using them for years and have never been let down.<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
